From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:01:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): long-press to select, copy and paste in the
 terminal on touch

The terminal draws to a canvas and xterm only selects with a mouse, so on a
phone there was no way to copy terminal output and no Paste control.

A still long-press selects the word under the finger (or offers Paste on a
blank cell), keeps the rest of the gesture to extend the selection, and
cancels the touchend so it never reaches the pane program as a click. Drag
handles adjust the range and scroll the scrollback past the edges. A small
menu offers Copy (through the existing terminal clipboard consent), Paste
(xterm's paste, so bracketed paste applies) and Select screen.

Not upstream yet: to be proposed after an issue is filed, as a follow-up
to the extra-keys row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
